# Walkthrough - Performance & Concurrency Optimization

I have implemented and verified a series of optimizations to resolve the 1 FPS UI degradation and high CPU usage issues.

## Key Accomplishments

### 1. UI Thread Optimization (GUI Fluidity)
- **O(1) Counters**: Added [loadedCount](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h#70-71) property to [ScrollBenchImageModel](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h#15-170).
- **Diagnostics Fix**: Replaced the O(N) item-scanning loop in [DiagnosticsMonitor](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/DiagnosticsMonitor.h#14-167) with a direct O(1) query.
- **Result**: GUI thread is no longer blocked by item counting, eliminating the "1 FPS" slowdown.

### 2. Task Weighting (CPU & I/O Protection)
- **Compute-Aware Scheduling**: Introduced a weight-based concurrency system in [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.h#44-139).
- **Weights**: RAW files and Videos now count as **4 tasks** (weight 4), while standard images count as 1.
- **Result**: Prevents compute-heavy decodes from overwhelming the system and starving the UI thread.

### 3. CPU-Aware Backoff (Dynamic Throttling)
- **Automatic Scaling**: The Adaptive I/O system now monitors system-wide CPU usage via [SystemMonitor](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/SystemMonitor.h#7-93).
- **Thresholds**: 
    - > 85% CPU: Concurrency limits are cut by 50%.
    - > 70% CPU: Concurrency limits are cut by 25%.
- **Result**: Ensures the application automatically yields resources when the system is under heavy load.

### 4. Restored Viewport Culling
- **Protocol Normalization**: Fixed a mismatch in [VisibleRangeManager.h](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/VisibleRangeManager.h) where `image://async/` protocols were preventing viewport items from being correctly identified.
- **Prioritized Admission**: Refined [processStagedRequests](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.cpp#506-644) to strictly reserve its "burst" capacity for visible items, ensuring the current view loads first even during heavy background activity.

### 5. Robust Build System
- **Process Cleanup**: Enhanced [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1) to more aggressively kill running app instances.
- **Lock Detection**: Implemented exclusive file access checks to prevent build failures due to locked binaries.
- **Post-Build Verification**: Added SHA256 hash verification to confirm that the build produced a fresh binary and report its status to the user.

